WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.179
Careful ablations on the Traffic benchmark tell us
which design choices matter.

00:00:05.259 --> 00:00:11.171
Reconstructing the current window from a past one
clearly beats plain self-reconstruction,

00:00:11.251 --> 00:00:13.368
validating the core Siamese idea.

00:00:13.448 --> 00:00:19.426
The masking ratio has a sweet spot around
twenty-five percent: masking only fifteen percent

00:00:19.506 --> 00:00:22.688
makes the task too easy to teach anything useful,

00:00:22.768 --> 00:00:26.216
while masking seventy-five percent makes it too hard.

00:00:26.296 --> 00:00:30.942
Lineage embeddings deliver consistent gains over
random initialization,

00:00:31.022 --> 00:00:36.867
and adding more of them keeps improving results on
Electricity and Traffic up to a point,

00:00:36.947 --> 00:00:42.060
confirming that explicitly modeling multiple
temporal distances is worthwhile.
